/* =============================================================================
   scrOverview -> OnVisible   (screen property: paste into the formula bar)

   ACCESS (change request 23.09.26): admins see everyone, line managers see
   only the people who named them as line manager, nobody else gets in.
   varIsAdmin comes from OnStart (People.IsAdmin). varIsLineManager is worked
   out HERE, from Alignments.LineManagerEmail (typed in by each person when
   they respond), not in OnStart, so that a missing or misnamed column can only
   break the admin screens - in OnStart it would take the whole app down.
   Anyone who is neither sees a no-access panel instead of the page.

   The data build itself lives in btnRefreshOverview.OnSelect (and, identically,
   in btnRefreshSubs.OnSelect on scrSubmissions). Select() runs it, so a visit
   and a press of "Refresh data" do exactly the same thing. A copy of that
   formula is in paste/admin-rebuild.powerfx.
   ============================================================================ */
/* NO Navigate HERE. Studio rejected it in this OnVisible ("Navigate cannot
   be used here since it would automatically always navigate away from this
   screen"), both chained in an If branch and on its own as
   If(Not (varIsAdmin Or varIsLineManager), Navigate(scrLanding)). So the
   screen does not send anyone away: its content (conContent) is Visible only
   to an admin or a line manager, everyone else sees the no-access panel with
   a Back to home button, and the data build below only runs when the check
   passes. */
Set(varIsLineManager, Not IsBlank(LookUp('RolePreference Alignments', LineManagerEmail = varUserEmail).EmployeeID));
If(varIsAdmin Or varIsLineManager, Set(varStaffTab, Coalesce(varStaffTab, "All")); Select(btnRefreshOverview))
